# Why this file exists — measured on this repo, not inherited.
#
# setuptools' legacy sdist default matches only `tests/test*.py`. It therefore
# omitted `tests/conftest.py` and `tests/__init__.py`. conftest.py defines the
# fixtures most of the shipped suite depends on, so the suite that shipped
# inside the sdist could not run: installing the published 0.4.0 sdist and
# running its own tests/ gave **30 passed, 1 failed, 14 errors** — the errors
# all fixture lookups failing at setup across test_awards, test_clr and
# test_tlr.
#
# The single FAILURE is a second, independent omission and the reason this file
# ships docs/ as well: tests/test_tlr.py::test_schema_doc_matches_canonical is
# an anti-drift guard that reads docs/CANONICAL_SCHEMA.md, and the sdist did not
# carry it. `recursive-include tests *.py` alone would leave that test failing
# inside the tarball.
#
# This reproduces ONLY from a clean checkout. A local `python -m build` in a
# working tree that already has `cdfidata.egg-info/` reuses the stale
# SOURCES.txt, which lists conftest.py, and produces a CORRECT sdist. Since
# `*.egg-info/` is gitignored, CI never has that seed — so the artifact CI ships
# is broken while the one a maintainer builds by hand looks fine. Verified: the
# file list of the 0.4.0 sdist on PyPI is identical to a fresh-clone build.
#
# SEVENTH instance of this defect in the portfolio: sbic-tracker, oz-tracker,
# cdfi-fund-tracker and nmtc-mapper hit it first, then cdfi-benchmark and
# hmda-analyzer as five and six. This repo is the third of a four-repo sweep;
# nmtc-application-builder follows as the eighth. (Do not copy this ordinal
# forward unchanged -- four files all claiming to be the fifth is how the count
# stops being evidence.) The fix was written four times and propagated nowhere,
# so this change is paired with a `test-sdist` job
# in release.yml that unpacks the built tarball and runs ITS suite. The
# MANIFEST.in is only what makes that job pass; the job is what stops this from
# silently regressing. Packaging that is never installed from is packaging that
# is never verified.
recursive-include tests *.py

include README.md
include CHANGELOG.md
include CONTRIBUTING.md
include pyproject.toml

# Not documentation-for-its-own-sake: the shipped suite reads this file. See the
# test_schema_doc_matches_canonical note above.
include docs/CANONICAL_SCHEMA.md

# pyproject.toml is load-bearing for the shipped suite beyond metadata: it
# carries [tool.pytest.ini_options], which registers the `live` marker that
# `-m "not live"` deselects on. Without it in the tarball, a test-sdist run
# emits PytestUnknownMarkWarning and --strict-markers turns that into an error.

global-exclude *.pyc
global-exclude __pycache__/*
